se,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Lyntris Inc. operates as a defense technology company that designs, develops, and provides connectivity solutions for the battlespace in the United States and internationally. The company offers solutions across the four domains of the connected battlespace: space, air, land, and sea. The company offers Sensor Architecture, a sensor to capture output, including embedded software, waveform optimization, and data translation; Sensor Hardware, the design and production of sensor subsystems and antenna systems that deliver wideband throughput, resilient narrowband, and simultaneous multi-band capabilities, with integrated radar, power, and thermal management; and Data and Software, a platform that ingests, fuses, and visualizes data, supporting C2 and mission execution, and enabling readiness, autonomy, and sustained operations. The company was incorporated in 2026 and is based in Falls Church, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian  Morrison | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $262,511 (FY2025)","financial_summary":["Lyntris Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.6B market cap on $389M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The company is burning through $28M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 1.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 91% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.91404833836858},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $149.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (39% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Lyntris (LYNX) Capitalizes on Mission-Critical Tech Across High-Priority Programs","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/lyntris-lynx-capitalizes-mission-critical-174904067.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794332944